  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nWeak troughing will develop over middle Ohio Valley tonight into\nMonday. With deep moisture remaining in place, any showers that\ndevelop could produce high rainfall rates. Guidance seems a bit\nuncertain on the coverage of the showers, likely due to extensive\ncloud cover and a lack of significant instability. However, believe\nwe will eventually get convective initiation under the broad \nconvergent flow with scattered showers becoming more numerous  \nthrough the evening.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2). \nWeak surface low pressure will wobble over the lower Great Lakes\nwhile upper troughing persists across the region. This will result in\nextensive cloud cover for mid summer along with near normal to a bit\nbelow normal temperatures through Tuesday. Clouds will decrease on\nWednesday as the trough weakens.",
